    <div class="legal-content">
      <h2>1. General Provisions and Controller Details</h2>
      <p>This Personal Data Processing Policy sets out the principal conditions for the processing of personal data in connection with the operation of the website “Bella Rybka — Psychology, Counselling, Authorship” at <a href="https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/</a> (hereinafter the “Website”) and the consideration of voluntary enquiries.</p>
      <p>The personal data controller is Rybka Bella Shamilievna, a natural person carrying out activities in Georgia. Contact email address for enquiries concerning personal data processing: <a href="mailto:x88tsar@gmail.com">x88tsar@gmail.com</a>. Postal address for correspondence: 19 Pirosmani Street, Batumi 6010, Georgia.</p>
      <p>When processing personal data, the controller complies with the applicable requirements of the Georgian Law on Personal Data Protection, other applicable provisions and the principles of lawfulness, purpose specification, data minimisation and proportionality of processing.</p>
      <h2>2. Categories of Data Subjects and Personal Data</h2>
      <p>Website visitors: technical data arising from access to the web resource, including the IP address, time and URL of the request, browser and device information, technical headers and, where protective mechanisms are applied, identifiers and information about information-security events.</p>
      <p>Persons sending messages: an email address or profile identifier in a communication service, name or pseudonym (if provided), the content of the enquiry and attachments sent at the sender’s initiative.</p>
      <p>Persons mentioned in published materials: personal data only where their publication has an applicable legal basis and complies with the law.</p>
      <p>The public part of the Website has no forms requesting health information or other special categories of personal data. Sending such information in ordinary correspondence without necessity is not recommended.</p>
      <h2>3. Purposes and Legal Bases of Processing</h2>
      <p>Providing access to the Website, ensuring its functionality and network security, technical diagnostics and counteracting misuse. Where applicable, the legal basis is the controller’s legitimate interest in ensuring the functioning and protection of the Website, subject to the rights and legitimate interests of data subjects.</p>
      <p>Considering voluntarily submitted enquiries, preparing and sending responses and, in the case of cooperation enquiries, communicating at the pre-contractual stage. The legal basis depends on the nature of the enquiry and may include taking steps at the data subject’s request prior to entering into a contract or a legitimate interest in conducting the relevant communication.</p>
      <p>Publishing materials containing information about third parties is permissible only where an appropriate legal basis exists. The controller does not carry out advertising profiling of visitors or use external web analytics.</p>
      <h2>4. Processing Operations and Data Recipients</h2>
      <p>Depending on the specific purpose, operations may include collection, transmission, recording of technical events, storage, viewing, use, restriction of access and erasure of data. Technical processing of network requests is predominantly automated. Correspondence is processed directly by the controller without establishing a separate register of enquiries.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare Pages is used to host and deliver pages. The provider may process technical information relating to requests to the Website. GitHub is used to store the source code and is not intended to collect data from ordinary visitors.</p>
      <p>The email address <a href="mailto:x88tsar@gmail.com">x88tsar@gmail.com</a> (Google/Gmail) is used to receive messages; communication is also possible through external Telegram and Instagram services at the sender’s initiative. These services process data in the course of providing their own services and under their own terms. Disclosure to public authorities is possible in cases established by applicable law.</p>
      <h2>5. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>The controller has not installed analytics, advertising or marketing cookies. Depending on the Cloudflare security mechanisms enabled, technical cookies, including __cf_bm and cf_clearance, may be used to verify requests and provide security.</p>
      <p>Description of Cloudflare mechanisms: <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/</a>. If other technologies requiring the data subject’s consent by law are introduced, relevant information and a consent mechanism will be provided before their use begins.</p>
      <h2>6. International Transfers of Personal Data</h2>
      <p>When using the international infrastructure of Cloudflare, Google and communication services, personal data may be processed outside Georgia. The controller takes into account the applicable requirements of Article 37 of the Georgian Law on Personal Data Protection concerning the legal bases and safeguards for international data transfers.</p>
      <p>The providers’ terms of data processing are set out in their official documents. An ordinary visit to an external link constitutes an independent interaction between the visitor and the relevant resource.</p>
      <h2>7. Retention Periods and Erasure</h2>
      <p>Technical information is processed for periods necessary to deliver pages, provide information security or carry out technical diagnostics, or for periods required by law. Specific retention periods for technical records depend on Cloudflare’s functions and terms; no single fixed period is established for all categories.</p>
      <p>Correspondence may be retained in email or a messaging service for the time necessary to consider the enquiry, continue communication, fulfil obligations or protect legitimate interests. Once the relevant grounds cease to apply, the controller deletes messages accessible to her, subject to exceptions established by law. Retention periods for data and backup copies held by service providers are determined by their terms and the law.</p>
      <h2>8. Organisational and Technical Security Measures</h2>
      <p>The controller uses a secure HTTPS connection, restricts access to Website management tools and work correspondence, and takes proportionate measures to protect accounts and data. Security measures are reviewed in light of changes in the technologies used and processing risks.</p>
      <h2>9. Rights of Data Subjects and Enquiry Procedure</h2>
      <p>A data subject may exercise the rights provided by applicable law, including the rights to receive information on processing and access to data, request rectification, completion, blocking, erasure or cessation of processing, withdraw consent where relevant, and challenge the controller’s actions.</p>
      <p>To exercise these rights, an enquiry should be sent to <a href="mailto:x88tsar@gmail.com">x88tsar@gmail.com</a>. Where necessary, the controller may request the minimum information required to identify the applicant. Response periods and grounds for restricting rights are determined by law; in the cases specified, Georgian law provides a period of 10 working days, extendable on lawful grounds.</p>
      <p>In the event of an alleged infringement of rights, the data subject may apply to the State Audit Office of Georgia and/or a court.</p>
      <h2>10. Review and Publication of the Policy</h2>
      <p>The Policy is updated when the purposes, legal bases, data categories, recipients or methods of processing change. The current version and its amendment date are published at <a href="https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/personal-data-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/personal-data-policy/</a>.</p>
    </div>
